2026-09-08T11:20:00Z ADVANCED - built + dispatched golden-set-pin-criterion for ISS-093 (high, the sole high open issue, and recorded BINDING on gate condition 4). ROOT CAUSE, measured before fixing: the filter rejected tokens "unique in the corpus retrieval scores", but that corpus is only 3,099 words across all 23 sessions (~135 each), so ordinary words land in one summary BY CHANCE and register as rare - should/will/you/people/paths/skills/living were ALL page-unique while none are turns-unique, and flywire (a real brand) is unique in both. That is why 13 of 17 rejections fired on function words. FIX: compute uniqueness over the turns corpus (217,980 words, ~70x larger); pin vocabulary 921 -> 159 and the survivors are the intended kind (shagun, handa, italia, provident, hrd, nationalized, 700). Second condition kept unchanged and still right: the token must also appear in the target page text, since a rare word is only a shortcut if the retriever can see it. Applied via a new --refilter path, NOT regeneration: the defect is in the criterion not the questions, so the same 92 candidates judged correctly give a different set - no API spend, and every question the previous checker human-read survives unchanged. RESULT: recall@5 0.307 (a biased floor) -> 0.391 (unbiased, exactly the combined figure the previous run predicted), control 0.187 -> 0.217, lift +0.120 -> +0.174, 56 misses, still INFORMATIVE, filter bias now structurally none. I CHECKED THE GOOD NEWS HARDEST: 0 of 92 rejected looks like a dead filter, so I verified it still fires on a synthetic question naming a rare entity - it does; the model complied with the prompt and the 17 earlier rejections were all false positives. Asked the checker to attack that result harder than I could. Disclosed: page-corpus pin rose 0.0% -> 18.5% and that is EXPECTED (the old 0.0% was tautological); the diagnostics deliberately do NOT match the filter criterion, because making them identical would recreate the ISS-092 tautology. gen-golden-set.mjs hit 353 LOC vs a 300 budget so the corpus/criterion/provenance/refilter code moved to scripts/lib/golden-set-build.mjs - a move, not a rewrite, kept separate from golden-set-diagnostics.mjs on purpose. Does NOT unblock condition 4: the sibling-session ambiguity precondition is untouched. Committed 6055634.
